{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/compiletimesafety"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"role":"article","title":"Compile-Time Dimension Type Safety","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Extending the Framework","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use generic constraints to make sure your APIs only ever receive the right kind of quantity."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit"},{"text":" carries a compile-time dimension type through its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dimension"},{"text":" associated type. That type is a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/DimensionProtocol"},{"text":"-conforming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"struct from the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension"},{"text":" namespace, such as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/length"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time"},{"text":". Because the compiler can see this type, it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reject dimension mismatches ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when you build your app"}]},{"text":" instead of when it runs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Historically, dimensions were only checked at runtime. With compile-time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constraints, a function that declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“only lengths, please”"}]},{"text":" is enforced by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Swift type checker.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Constrain-a-Generic-to-a-Dimension","type":"heading","text":"Constrain a Generic to a Dimension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write a generic function or protocol requirement over a unit type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U: MathUnit"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then constrain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U.Dimension"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"where"},{"text":" clause:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Math","","\/\/ This method only accepts quantities of length.","func measureDistance<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Bool","where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length {","    distance.value > 0","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Passing-the-Correct-Units","type":"heading","text":"Passing the Correct Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The built-in units in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"text":" are already parameterized by their dimension.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Passing a length unit compiles cleanly:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let radius = Quantity(value: 500, unit: Units.meter)","measureDistance(radius) \/\/ Compiles perfectly! ✅"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Preventing-Mismatched-Units","type":"heading","text":"Preventing Mismatched Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing a quantity of a different dimension is a compile-time error:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let timeLimit = Quantity(value: 30, unit: Units.minute)","measureDistance(timeLimit) \/\/ ✗ ERROR: 'time' is not 'length'"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Runtime-Checks-for-Dynamic-Dimensions","type":"heading","text":"Runtime Checks for Dynamic Dimensions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not every quantity has a static dimension. Custom dimensions created at runtime","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions"},{"text":") use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown"},{"text":" as their type-level","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parameter. For those, the compiler can’t help—so ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"},{"text":" keeps its runtime","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"safety net. Operations that combine quantities verify that dimensions match and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raise a runtime ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preconditionFailure"},{"text":" if they don’t:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\", dimension: usdDimension, converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])","let userUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"user\", dimension: userDimension, converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ Traps at runtime: USD ≠ users","let revenue = Quantity(value: 100, unit: usdUnit) + Quantity(value: 3, unit: userUnit)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Applying-Constraints-at-the-Protocol-Level","type":"heading","text":"Applying Constraints at the Protocol Level"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can attach the same constraint to a protocol so every conformer enforces it:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["protocol DistanceMeasurer {","    func measure<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Double","    where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length","}","","\/\/ All built-in length units satisfy this automatically:","struct RangeFinder: DistanceMeasurer {","    func measure<U: MathUnit>(_ distance: Quantity<U>) -> Double","    where U.Dimension == MathDimension.length {","        distance.converted(to: Units.meter).value","    }","}","","let width = Quantity(value: 10, unit: Units.foot)","RangeFinder().measure(width) \/\/ 3.048"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Whats-Next","type":"heading","text":"What’s Next?"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See the full list of compile-time dimensions in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Combine compile-time safety with your own domain in "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/DimensionProtocol":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DimensionProtocol"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DimensionProtocol"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A protocol representing a type-level identifier for a physical dimension.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/DimensionProtocol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/math\/dimensionprotocol","title":"DimensionProtocol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension","title":"MathDimension","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MathDimension","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MathDimension","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A namespace containing type-level structures for compile-time physical dimension verification."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/Units":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A namespace of ready-made units for every dimension in the framework."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","url":"\/documentation\/math\/units","title":"Units","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Units","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Units"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/unknown":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/unknown","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The compile-time dimension type used for dimensions that don’t have a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"static type, such as custom dimensions created at runtime.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unknown","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MathDimension.unknown","role":"symbol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform type-safe dimensional analysis and unit conversion in your Swift app."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/math","title":"Math"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/length":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"length","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"length","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type representing length."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/length","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/length","title":"MathDimension.length"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/time":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"time","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/time","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type representing time."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"time","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MathDimension.time","role":"symbol"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathUnit":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MathUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MathUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit of measurement, such as a meter, a second, or a US dollar."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathunit","title":"MathUnit"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/CustomDimensions":{"role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Extend ","type":"text"},{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else